OL,3,ARussell Brand prison message denying
OL,4,Arape 'appalling' and being
OL,5,Ainvestigated, No 10 says
OL,6,
OL,7,FA message by Russell Brand to his
OL,8,Ffollowers in which he claimed innocence
OL,9,Ffor his sexual offences was "clearly
OL,10,Fappalling" and is being urgently
OL,11,Finvestigated, Downing Street has said.
OL,13,FThe comedian is currently serving a
OL,14,F10-and-half-year prison sentence after
OL,15,Fbeing convicted of rape and three
OL,16,Fcounts of sexual assault.
OL,18,FHis wife Laura read out a message from
OL,19,Fhim on their Sunday Service show on
OL,20,FYouTube, in which the convicted rapist
OL,21,Fclaimed: "I am not guilty of the
OL,22,Foffences I have been jailed for."
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,303,300,200,140,0,100
