OL,3,ABarristers must stop using rape myths
OL,4,Ain trials, justice secretary says
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe justice secretary has called for
OL,7,Fnew rules to prevent barristers from
OL,8,Fusing rape myths to defend their
OL,9,Fclients in the wake of the Russell
OL,10,FBrand trial.
OL,12,FAs first reported by the Times, in a
OL,13,Fletter to the Bar Standards Bar (BSB),
OL,14,FAlex Norris said it was "unacceptable"
OL,15,Fto "perpetuate myths" about victims in
OL,16,Fcourt and disciplinary action could be
OL,17,Ftaken against those who do so.
OL,19,FIn his closing speech, Brand's defence
OL,20,Fbarrister, Ian Winter KC, questioned
OL,21,Fwhy his client's accusers had not
OL,22,Ffought back.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,0,100
